{"version":"ai-mcq-bank-v2-la-batch15-high-quality-rewritten-affected-2026-05-22-stem-fixed-inequality-rendering-fixed-student-facing-qc-2026-05-31-pt-foundations-2026-06-11-pt-batch2-foundations-counting-2026-06-11-pt-batch3-counting-probability-rules-2026-06-11-pt-batch4-conditioning-2026-06-11-pt-batch5-random-variables-2026-06-11-pt-batch6-discrete-distributions-2026-06-11-pt-batch7-distribution-foundations-2026-06-11-pt-batch8-continuous-expectation-2026-06-11-pt-batch9-non-week7-expectation-transform-2026-06-11-pt-batch10-non-week7-process-summary-2026-06-11-pt-batch11-non-week7-final-summary-shape-2026-06-11-quality-round1-2026-06-14-quality-round2-2026-06-14-quality-round3-2026-06-14-quality-round4-deep-2026-06-14+quality-round5-difficulty-2026-06-14+quality-round6-expression-2026-06-14+quality-round7-answer-cue-2026-06-14+quality-round8-answer-shape-2026-06-14+quality-round9-answer-position-2026-06-14+quality-round10-template-padding-2026-06-14+quality-round11-generic-stems-2026-06-14+quality-round12-deterministic-cleanup-2026-06-15+quality-pilot-deep-rework-2026-06-15+v3-2026-10-04+upright-2026-10-04+v3-2026-10-04+v3-2026-10-06+v3-2026-10-06+qa-fixes-2026-10-08","concept_id":"Year-1/2a-Math-III-Analysis/big-o-and-little-o-notations.html","concept":{"concept_id":"Year-1/2a-Math-III-Analysis/big-o-and-little-o-notations.html","questions":[{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_big_o_and_little_o_notations_c490e3b9_001","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What does $f(x)=O(g(x))$ as $x\\to a$ require?","options":["The limit $f(x)/g(x)$ must equal $1$.","There exist $M \\gt 0$ and $\\delta \\gt 0$ such that $|f(x)| \\le Mg(x)$ in a punctured neighbourhood of $a$.","The function $g$ must be negative near $a$.","The function $f$ must be identically zero on a punctured neighbourhood of $a$, so that $|f(x)|\\le g(x)$ there."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"b1ed990e8afc001f98737674","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_big_o_and_little_o_notations_c490e3b9_002","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What does $f(x)=o(g(x))$ as $x\\to a$ require?","options":["$\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to a}\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)} = 0$","$\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to a}\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)} = 1$","$|f(x)| \\ge g(x)$ near $a$","$g(x) = 0$ throughout a neighbourhood of $a$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"1c58d7840b95c0ac43d3562b","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_big_o_and_little_o_notations_c490e3b9_003","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"As $x\\to 0$, which statement about $x^2$ and $x$ is true?","options":["$x^2$ is $O(x)$ but not $o(x)$.","$x^2$ is neither $O(x)$ nor $o(x)$.","$x^2$ is both $O(x)$ and $o(x)$.","$x$ is $o(x^2)$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"e4a1d087905571bcceea4847","time_limit":35},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_big_o_and_little_o_notations_c490e3b9_004","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"As $x\\to 0$, what is stated about $\\sin(x^2)$ relative to $x^2$?","options":["$\\sin(x^2)$ is $o(x^2)$.","$\\sin(x^2)$ is not $O(x^2)$.","$x^2$ is not comparable to $\\sin(x^2)$ in any way.","$\\sin(x^2)$ is $O(x^2)$ but not $o(x^2)$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"b6efc9601db062e89e18342f","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_big_o_and_little_o_notations_c490e3b9_005","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which notation makes a stronger assertion?","options":["Big-$O$","Little-$o$","They are always equivalent","Neither notation compares functions"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"5d50a5f49b9875a106ce52e0","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_big_o_and_little_o_notations_c490e3b9_006","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"If $f(x)\\sim g(x)$ as $x\\to a$, what big-$O$ relations are stated?","options":["$f(x) = O(g(x))$ and $g(x) = O(f(x))$","Only $f(x) = o(g(x))$","Only $g(x) = o(f(x))$","Neither function is big-$O$ of the other"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9559aa1c1f4833c73c1e4599","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_big_o_and_little_o_notations_c490e3b9_007","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"As $x\\to 0$, what is true for $f(x) = 3x^2$ and $g(x) = x^2$?","options":["$f(x) = O(g(x))$ but $f(x)\\ne o(g(x))$","$f(x) = o(g(x))$","$f(x)$ is not $O(g(x))$.","$g(x) = o(f(x))$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"208e4c89afa9028c93670283","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_big_o_and_little_o_notations_c490e3b9_008","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"As $x\\to 0$, what is true for $f(x) = x^3$ and $g(x) = x^2$?","options":["$g(x) = o(f(x))$","$f(x)$ is not $O(g(x))$","$f(x)/g(x)$ tends to $1$","$f(x) = o(g(x))$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"ebcacc43cb24f525348489af","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_big_o_and_little_o_notations_c490e3b9_009","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which of the following big-O or little-o claims, with the limiting directions shown, is false?","options":["$\\sin x=o(x)$ as $x\\to+\\infty$","$2^x=O(x^2)$ as $x\\to+\\infty$","$x^2=o(x)$ as $x\\to0$","$x=O(\\sin x)$ as $x\\to0$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9241d579b3093cd1270f7469","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_big_o_and_little_o_notations_c490e3b9_010","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Why does $f(x) = O(g(x))$ not by itself imply $f(x) = o(g(x))$?","options":["Big-$O$ requires the quotient to tend to $0$.","Big-$O$ only gives a bound, while little-$o$ requires the quotient to tend to $0$.","Little-$o$ is weaker than big-$O$.","The two notations mean the same thing, so a bound already forces the quotient to tend to $0$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"0bf0f3b61a52bab144f9f9c2","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_big_o_and_little_o_notations_c490e3b9_011","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"As $x\\to 0$, is $x = O(x^2)$?","options":["Yes, because $x/x^2\\to 0$.","No, because $|x|/x^2 = 1/|x|$ is not bounded near $0$.","Yes, because every real function is $O(x^2)$ near the point $0$.","No, because $x^2$ is strictly negative near $0$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"f8fa37cf6ee3d23add3e9992","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_big_o_and_little_o_notations_c490e3b9_012","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $f(x)=o(x^2)$ and $g(x)=o(x^3)$ as $x\\to0$. Which statement about $(f(x)+g(x))^2$ is guaranteed?","options":["It is $O(x^6)$ as $x\\to0$.","It is $o(x^4)$ as $x\\to0$.","It is $o(x^5)$ as $x\\to0$.","It is $o(x^6)$ as $x\\to0$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9094f5c35229e9421164cbab","time_limit":30},{"id":"expansion_big_o_and_little_o_notations_013","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What kind of bound defines $f(x)=O(g(x))$ as $x\\to a$?","options":["$|f(x)|\\le Mg(x)$ near $a$ for some $M \\gt 0$","$f(x)/g(x)\\to\\infty$","$f(x)=g(x)$ for all $x$","$g(x)=0$ in every punctured neighbourhood"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"ca761a21edc7a1e85865ea68","time_limit":25},{"id":"expansion_big_o_and_little_o_notations_014","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What limit defines $f(x)=o(g(x))$ as $x\\to a$?","options":["$\\lim_{x\\to a}f(x)/g(x)=1$","$\\lim_{x\\to a}g(x)/f(x)=0$","$\\lim_{x\\to a}f(x)/g(x)=0$","$\\lim_{x\\to a}f(x)=\\infty$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"086bf498b630e1a934f74a43","time_limit":20},{"id":"expansion_big_o_and_little_o_notations_015","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $a\\in\\mathbb{R}$ and $g(x)\\neq0$ near $a$. Which statement implies $f(x)=O(g(x))$ as $x\\to a$, but is not implied by it?","options":["$g(x)=O(f(x))$ as $x\\to a$","$|f(x)|\\ge c\\,|g(x)|$ near $a$ for some $c>0$","$f(x)=o(g(x))$ as $x\\to a$","$f(a)=g(a)$ at the point $a$ itself"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"336f01251bcb5d03304c9bf6","time_limit":35},{"id":"expansion_big_o_and_little_o_notations_016","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"As $x\\to0$, which statement is true for $x^3$ relative to $x^2$?","options":["$x^3=o(x^2)$","$x^2=o(x^3)$","$x^3$ is not $O(x^2)$","$x^3/x^2\\to1$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"b04bba7c1dfc5912c928ec8b","time_limit":25},{"id":"expansion_big_o_and_little_o_notations_017","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"As $x\\to0$, which statement is true for $x^2$ relative to $x^2$?","options":["$x^2=o(x^2)$, hence also $x^2=O(x^2)$","$x^2=O(x^2)$ but $x^2\\ne o(x^2)$","$x^2\\ne O(x^2)$, since $x^2\\to0$","Neither, as $x^2/x^2$ is undefined at $0$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"2a7c5caf1143ffb4be7b8429","time_limit":30},{"id":"expansion_big_o_and_little_o_notations_018","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"As $x\\to0$, why is $5x^3=o(x)$?","options":["Because $5x^3/x\\to5$","Because $x$ is never positive","Because $5x^3/x=5x^2\\to0$","Because little-$o$ ignores ratios"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"a50965f20c335c33155b3ea9","time_limit":20},{"id":"expansion_big_o_and_little_o_notations_019","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"If $f(x)\\sim g(x)$ as $x\\to a$, which big-$O$ relations follow?","options":["Only $f(x)=o(g(x))$","Only $g(x)=o(f(x))$","Neither function can be bounded by the other","$f(x)=O(g(x))$ and $g(x)=O(f(x))$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9f10bc0feee3ee5d38bd2b42","time_limit":30},{"id":"expansion_big_o_and_little_o_notations_020","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"As $x\\to0$, what is true for $f(x)=5x^4$ and $g(x)=x^2$?","options":["$f(x)=o(g(x))$","$g(x)=o(f(x))$","$f(x)/g(x)\\to5$","$f(x)$ is not $O(g(x))$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9ff66e5aba659ded158dcdd9","time_limit":30}]}}